# Official documentation is binding (auth / WebDAV / previews)

This rule exists because inventing auth shortcuts caused real harm (Nextcloud user lockout). **No exceptions.**

## Allowed account paths

1. **Login Flow v2** and/or **username + app password** over OkHttp Basic Auth (store app password in EncryptedSharedPreferences).
2. **Nextcloud Files Android Single Sign-On** via the official Android-SingleSignOn library / `NextcloudAPI`, when the user depends on the Nextcloud Files app — as documented in the Android client APIs page.

There is **no** approved “SSO token as OkHttp Basic Auth” bridge.

## Hard guarantee

For **any** change that touches Nextcloud login, credentials, WebDAV, OCS, `/core/preview`, or how secrets leave the device:

1. **Read the official doc first** (fetch/open the canonical page in-session). Do not rely on memory or analogy.
2. **Cite the doc in chat** (URL + the constraint that applies) **before** writing or proposing code.
3. **Implement only what that doc allows.** If the doc does not describe a path, **stop and ask** — do not invent “equivalent” auth.
4. **One concern at a time** when the user asked for that workflow.

## Canonical references (use current “latest” / stable official pages)

- Nextcloud Login Flow (incl. v2): https://docs.nextcloud.com/server/latest/developer_manual/client_apis/LoginFlow/index.html
- Nextcloud WebDAV: https://docs.nextcloud.com/server/latest/developer_manual/client_apis/WebDAV/basic.html
- Nextcloud Android / SSO option: https://docs.nextcloud.com/server/latest/developer_manual/client_apis/android_library/index.html
- Android-SingleSignOn usage: https://github.com/nextcloud/Android-SingleSignOn (network via `NextcloudAPI` / Files stack)
- Android data at rest / EncryptedSharedPreferences (when storing secrets): Android developer docs current for the APIs in use.

## Explicitly forbidden

- Bypassing Login Flow with ad-hoc password handling that contradicts Login Flow (“client never stores the user password”; prefer app passwords from the flow).
- Claiming compliance without having opened the doc in that work session.
- Using an SSO / AccountManager **token as OkHttp Basic Auth** (or any undocumented credential remapping) for WebDAV or `/core/preview`.
- Reintroducing Files SSO **without** routing SSO account traffic through `NextcloudAPI` (or without a fresh docs check).

## Library thumbs (product constraint)

SSO accounts must share the same **LibraryPreviewGate** policy as Basic Auth (visible cells, settle delay, single-flight + spacing, Coil cache). SSO thumbs use the SSO Coil fetcher over a **reused** `NextcloudAPI`, not a parallel ungated path.

## If unsure

Match the official client pattern documented for that API. Prefer asking the user over shipping an undocumented auth path.
